-- title:
--   Cartier duality of p-divisible groups is stable under base change
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring and let $p,h$ be natural numbers. Let $G,G'$ be $p$-divisible groups over $R$ of parameters $p,h$ in the sense of the project's structure: each consists of a family of commutative, cocommutative Hopf $R$-algebras $G.\mathrm{level}\,v$ that are finite and free over $R$ of rank $p^{vh}$, together with surjective $R$-bialgebra maps $G.\mathrm{transition}\,v\colon G.\mathrm{level}(v+1)\to G.\mathrm{level}\,v$ whose kernel is the ideal generated by the image of the augmentation ideal under the $p^v$-fold multiplication map `nsmulAlgHom`. Assume $G.\mathrm{IsCartierDual}\,G'$, i.e. there exists a `CartierDuality` datum: $R$-bialgebra isomorphisms $G'.\mathrm{level}\,v \simeq \mathrm{CartierDual}_R(G.\mathrm{level}\,v)$ for every $v$ such that for all $x \in G'.\mathrm{level}(v+1)$ and $a \in G.\mathrm{level}(v+1)$ the pairing satisfies $\langle \mathrm{transition}_v x, \mathrm{transition}_v a\rangle = \langle x, [p]^{*}a\rangle$, where $[p]^{*}$ is `nsmulAlgHom` at $p$. Let $S$ be a nontrivial commutative $R$-algebra. The conclusion is that the base-changed $p$-divisible groups, whose levels are $S \otimes_R G.\mathrm{level}\,v$ and $S \otimes_R G'.\mathrm{level}\,v$ with transitions $\mathrm{id}_S \otimes \mathrm{transition}_v$, again satisfy $(G.\mathrm{baseChange}\,S).\mathrm{IsCartierDual}\,(G'.\mathrm{baseChange}\,S)$.
--
--   This is the compatibility of Cartier duality for $p$-divisible groups with base change along a ring map $R \to S$. It is used in the proof that the dimensions of a $p$-divisible group and of its Cartier dual sum to the height, where one reduces to a base ring over which the relevant modules are better behaved.
